# The design system is published to GitHub Packages, which requires a token for
# reads as well as writes — public packages included. So every install needs a
# credential: developer machines, CI and image builds alike.
#
# The credential is deliberately NOT in this file. pnpm 11 ignores an auth
# setting that comes from a project .npmrc and expands no environment variable
# in one, because this file is committed and a `${TOKEN}` here could be made to
# leak to an attacker-controlled registry. It has to come from a trusted source:
#
#   Local    one line in your own ~/.npmrc — see docs/design-system.md:
#            //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
#            then export NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=<a PAT with read:packages>.
#   CI       actions/setup-node writes exactly that line to a user-level file
#            and points NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG at it; NODE_AUTH_TOKEN on the
#            install step is the repository's own GITHUB_TOKEN.
#   Images   the same user-level line, with the token mounted as a BuildKit
#            secret for the one RUN that installs — never a layer, never a
#            build argument.
#
# What does belong here is the routing: which scope this registry serves. The
# scope must equal the GitHub organisation login, because GitHub Packages
# resolves a scope to an owner.
@ptv-mobility:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
